## UI Design Specification ##

**Website:** [Zonke.me](https://zonke.me/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
**Document:** UI/UX Design & Visual System Proposal
**Purpose:** Website redesign, visual consistency, improved usability, and updated platform functionality

---

## 1. Project Overview

The proposed UI design for **Zonke.me** focuses on creating a modern, professional, trustworthy, and user-friendly digital platform.

The design system will establish consistent standards across the website, including:

* Colors
* Typography
* Layout
* Navigation
* Buttons
* Cards
* Forms
* Images
* Icons
* Mobile responsiveness
* Payment gateway integration
* Cybersecurity job opportunities
* Freelance functionality
* Bounties
* Platform-specific content

The overall objective is to create a cohesive user experience that makes Zonke.me easier to navigate while clearly communicating its services and opportunities.

---

# 2. Design System

## 2.1 Colors

The primary visual direction will be based around a **blue-focused brand identity**, supported by purple, red, black, and white.

| Element                        | Design Direction |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------- |
| **Primary Brand Color**        | Blue             |
| **Primary Button Color**       | Light Blue       |
| **Background Color**           | White            |
| **Text Color**                 | Black            |
| **Card Color**                 | Purple           |
| **Border Color**               | Purple           |
| **Hover / Active State**       | Red              |
| **Error / Success Indicators** | Red              |

### Color Application

**Blue**

* Primary branding
* Navigation highlights
* Important interface elements
* Links
* Primary visual accents

**Light Blue**

* Primary buttons
* Calls to action
* Interactive elements

**White**

* Main website background
* Form backgrounds
* Clean content sections

**Black**

* Main headings
* Body text
* Important information

**Purple**

* Cards
* Supporting UI components
* Borders
* Secondary visual elements

**Red**

* Hover and active states
* Error messages
* Important alerts
* Validation feedback

The color system should remain consistent throughout the website to strengthen brand recognition and improve usability.

